> Simple and repeated roots have different local rates

The next fixed experiments use x0=2 and tolerance10⁻¹⁴. The simple-root function
is x²−2, with reference sqrt(2). The repeated-root control is(x−1)² with
derivative2(x−1), reference1. Its exact-arithmetic error halves on every update,
illustrating the multiplicity-two factor rather than quadratic convergence. All
plotted errors read actual inspected x values; no extra update loop is run.
Displaying log10(max(error,10⁻¹⁶)) makes the rounding floor explicit and is not
a measured extra iteration.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/newton_rates.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/newton_raphson.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto simple = dm::algorithms::newton_raphson_square_study(2, 1e-14, 100);
    auto repeated = dm::algorithms::newton_raphson_trace([](double x) {
        return (x - 1) * (x - 1);
    }, [](double x) {
        return 2 * (x - 1);
    }, 2, 1e-14, 100);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < simple.states.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(std::log10(std::max(simple.reference_errors[i], 1e-16)));
    }
    p.points(x, y, "simple root", {36, 105, 172}, 5);
    x.clear();
    y.clear();
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < repeated.steps.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(std::log10(std::max(std::abs(repeated.steps[i].x - 1), 1e-16)));
    }
    p.points(x, y, "double root", {192, 59, 50}, 4).title(
        "Actual reference errors: simple versus repeated root").x_label(
        "actual inspected state index").y_label("log10(max(reference error, 1e-16))").save_svg("build/newton_rates.svg");
    std::print("| function | actual updates | final residual | final reference error |\n| --- | ---: | ---: " "| ---: |\n| x squared minus2 | {} | {} | {} |\n| squared distance to1 | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               simple.trace.run.updates, simple.trace.run.result.residual,
               simple.reference_errors.back(), repeated.run.updates,
               repeated.run.result.residual,
               std::abs(repeated.run.result.root - 1));
}
```
